[center]
[size=6][b][color=#D6A24A]CIGAR[/color][/b][/size]
[size=4][b]Contextual Interactions for Skyrim[/b][/size]

[size=3][b][color=#E6B85C]ONE BUTTON. THE RIGHT ACTION. NO HOTKEY CLUTTER.[/color][/b][/size]
[/center]

[size=4][b][color=#D6A24A]Description[/color][/b][/size]

[color=#D4D4D8]
A heavily modded Skyrim ends up with dozens of hotkeys for actions that matter only in specific situations. CIGAR replaces them with on-screen prompts: when an action makes sense, a prompt appears, and [b][color=#E6B85C]one button performs the whole action[/color][/b]. When it does not, the prompt stays out of the way.
[/color]


[size=4][b][color=#D6A24A]Design Philosophy[/color][/b][/size]

[color=#D4D4D8]
Modern games such as [b]Red Dead Redemption 2, Monster Hunter, Hitman[/b] and [b]Assassin's Creed[/b] have more actions than buttons, so what a button does depends on context: what you look at, what you are doing, your equipment and whether you are in combat. CIGAR applies that design pattern to Skyrim, rebuilt around Skyrim's own mechanics rather than copied from any one game.
[/color]


[size=4][b][color=#D6A24A]Main Features[/color][/b][/size]

[color=#D4D4D8]
CIGAR is an [b]ESP-less SKSE plugin[/b]: nothing is added to your load order.

[center]
[b][color=#E6B85C]CONTEXT → PROMPT → ONE INPUT → COMPLETE ACTION[/color][/b]
[/center]

It is not a radial menu or a hotkey launcher. Each prompt is built for one situation, and anything that already works well with one button is left alone.
[/color]


[size=4][b][color=#D6A24A]What CIGAR Does[/color][/b][/size]

[color=#D4D4D8]
Most prompts work with Skyrim alone. Others appear only when the mod they drive is installed, and quietly stay away when it is not. CIGAR includes none of those mods' files. Prompts stay away while a SexLab or OStim scene plays the player.

[b]Daily life[/b]
- Undress / Get Dressed (bed, wardrobe, water)
- Sit, Lie Down, Lean on a wall, table or railing, Warm Hands at a fire
- Pass Time while resting or seated (hold)
- Drink at an inn or home while seated
- Observe a person or a distant view (hold to zoom)
- Bathe / Shower [i](Bathing in Skyrim - Renewed)[/i]
- Eat the cheapest suitable food when hungry [i](Survival Mode + Survival Mode Improved)[/i]
- Urinate / Defecate, never while bathing [i](Private Needs - Orgasm)[/i]
- Deflate [i](Fill Her Up Baka Edition)[/i]

[b]Gear and items[/b]
- Equip newly acquired gear (armor only when it beats what you wear, never over an enchanted piece)
- Read unknown spell tomes and quest notes
- Helmet off by default so your face shows; put it back on in combat
- Recharge an enchanted weapon with the best-fitting soul gem
- Apply the most valuable poison to a drawn weapon
- Drink the right potion for low health, stamina or magicka, poison, disease or water breathing
- Swap outfits with a mannequin in one hold; enchanted and tempered pieces move as they are

[b]Quests[/b]
- Track a quest when it gets a new objective
- Equip the shout the Greybeards ask for
- Party clothes for the Thalmor embassy party, and back again
- Choose an action in the kidnap room [i](BaboDialogue)[/i]

[b]Combat[/b]
- Ranged / Melee weapon swap by enemy distance
- Jujutsu: throw a blocking humanoid enemy; stamina and health damage are adjustable
- Lock On [i](True Directional Movement)[/i]
- Execute a stunned enemy [i](Valhalla Combat)[/i]
- Surrender at low health [i](Acheron; respects Yamete Kudasai's 3-minute rule)[/i]
- Wizard Warrior Mode on when you draw, off when you sheathe out of combat [i](The Wizard Warrior)[/i]

[b]Where prompts appear[/b]

In third person, prompts sit just ahead of your character's head, a little to the right; how far to the right is a setting. In first person they stay on your character. CIGAR keeps one invisible marker in each save for this; it is harmless if CIGAR is removed.

[b]Hotkeys CIGAR takes over[/b]

So that one key does not do two things, CIGAR can take a mod's own hotkey over. This is the [b]prompt only[/b] switch in the settings panel, [b]on by default[/b]; switching it off gives the key back.

- Acheron: the surrender key moves to F14
- Valhalla Combat: the execution key moves to F15
- Fill Her Up Baka Edition: the deflate hotkey is cleared
- Private Needs - Orgasm: its six hotkeys are cleared

The full prompt list, settings and details are in [b]README.md[/b] in the download.
[/color]

[size=4][b][color=#D6A24A]Built for Heavily Modded Skyrim[/color][/b][/size]

[color=#D4D4D8]
Too many useful mods need too many dedicated controls, and a gamepad runs out of buttons first. CIGAR treats [b]context as extra input space[/b], so you remember fewer controls and a modded game plays more like one designed game.

[center]
[b][color=#E6B85C]The system absorbs complexity.
The player plays the game.[/color][/b]
[/center]
[/color]


[size=4][b][color=#D6A24A]Installation Instructions[/color][/b][/size]

[color=#D4D4D8]
1. Install [b]SKSE64[/b].
2. Install [b]Address Library for SKSE Plugins[/b].
3. Install [b]SkyPrompt[/b] and its own requirements (SKSE Menu Framework, ImGui Icons).
4. Install CIGAR normally through your preferred mod manager.
5. Launch Skyrim through SKSE.

CIGAR is [b]ESP-less[/b] and does not require a new game. Updating from 2.x needs nothing special.
[/color]

[size=4][b][color=#D6A24A]Requirements[/color][/b][/size]

[color=#D4D4D8]
[b]Required[/b]

- Skyrim Special Edition / Anniversary Edition (tested on 1.6.1170)
- [url=https://skse.silverlock.org/]SKSE64[/url]
- [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/skyrimspecialedition/mods/32444]Address Library for SKSE Plugins[/url]
- [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/skyrimspecialedition/mods/148703]SkyPrompt[/url] (tested with 2.4.0; 2.3.15 works too)
- [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/skyrimspecialedition/mods/120352]SKSE Menu Framework[/url] (SkyPrompt requires it; it also hosts CIGAR's settings panel)

[b]Optional[/b] (each one enables its own prompts; none is needed to install CIGAR)

- [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/skyrimspecialedition/mods/135288]Bathing in Skyrim - Renewed[/url]
- [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/skyrimspecialedition/mods/51614]True Directional Movement[/url]
- [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/skyrimspecialedition/mods/64741]Valhalla Combat[/url]
- [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/skyrimspecialedition/mods/108159]Acheron[/url], and [url=https://www.loverslab.com/files/file/23123-yamete-kudasai/]Yamete Kudasai[/url] (LoversLab)
- Survival Mode (Creation Club, included with the current game) and [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/skyrimspecialedition/mods/78244]Survival Mode Improved - SKSE[/url]
- [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/skyrimspecialedition/mods/96876]Gourmet[/url]
- [url=https://subscribestar.adult/posts/118628]Fill Her Up Baka Edition[/url] (BakaFactory)
- [url=https://www.loverslab.com/files/file/39023-private-needs-orgasm/]Private Needs - Orgasm[/url] (LoversLab)
- [url=https://www.loverslab.com/files/file/17496-babodialogue/]BaboDialogue[/url] (BakaFactory, LoversLab)
- [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/skyrimspecialedition/mods/14890]The Wizard Warrior - Spellsword Magic Combat Evolved[/url]

[b]Input[/b]

Keyboard and mouse, or a gamepad through SkyPrompt's own gamepad buttons. CIGAR's key settings change the keyboard keys only.

Third-party mods, assets and trademarks remain the property of their respective authors. CIGAR only interacts with them at runtime and includes none of their files.
[/color]

[size=4][b][color=#D6A24A]Language[/color][/b][/size]

[color=#D4D4D8]
Prompts, notifications and the settings panel are in [b]English or Korean[/b]. CIGAR follows your game's language automatically; you can switch it in the settings panel. Item, quest and character names come from your game, so a translated game shows its own names inside English prompts.

[b]Prompts show ??? (question marks)?[/b] That is SkyPrompt's font, not a CIGAR setting: give SkyPrompt a font for your language.

[b]More answers (the ??? fix step by step, Observe, OStim, drinking, SSE 1.5.97) are in the pinned FAQ post in the Posts tab.[/b]
[/color]


[size=4][b][color=#D6A24A]Known Issues[/color][/b][/size]

[color=#D4D4D8]
- [b]Jujutsu does nothing until someone has died since the game was loaded.[/b] After the first death it works normally.
- [b]Execute can miss the first press.[/b] Press again.
- [b]The helmet comes off at once, without an animation.[/b]
- [b]A weapon enchantment stays after End Wizard Warrior[/b] until it runs out. That is The Wizard Warrior's own design.
- [b]Mannequins:[/b] tested with the Unofficial Patch and Another Mannequin Script Fix.
[/color]

[size=4][b][color=#D6A24A]Design Inspiration & Shout Outs[/color][/b][/size]

[color=#D4D4D8]
Thanks to the developers of [b]SKSE, CommonLibSSE-NG[/b] and [b]SkyPrompt[/b], to the authors of the mods CIGAR works with, and to the Skyrim modding community.

Design references: [b]Red Dead Redemption 2, Monster Hunter, Hitman, Assassin's Creed, Tekken[/b] and [b]Guilty Gear[/b]. CIGAR takes the design principle behind a solution and rebuilds it for Skyrim; it does not reproduce any one game.
[/color]


[size=4][b][color=#D6A24A]Open Source & Independent Development[/color][/b][/size]

[color=#D4D4D8]
CIGAR is open source under the [b]GNU General Public License v3.0 or later[/b], as required by CommonLibSSE-NG. The license is [b]LICENSE.txt[/b] in the download, with third-party notices in [b]THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.txt[/b]. [b]Source code:[/b] [url=https://github.com/kkw1010-dev/HKT]github.com/kkw1010-dev/HKT[/url]

Forks and modified builds must follow the GPL and must not be presented as official CIGAR releases; official releases are the ones on this page and the repository's GitHub releases. Contextual interaction is a general game-design pattern, so a mod that solves the same problem with its own code is independent work, not a fork.
[/color]


[size=4][b][color=#D6A24A]Disclaimer — AI-Assisted Development[/color][/b][/size]

[color=#D4D4D8]
[b][color=#FFFFFF]Yes. This project contains AI-generated code.[/color][/b] Most of CIGAR was written with [b]Claude Opus 5.5[/b] under human design, direction, review, in-game testing and final QA. I do not consider AI-written code inferior when the goal, architecture and acceptance criteria are clear and the result is tested in the game.

[b][color=#E6B85C]If AI-assisted development is, by itself, unacceptable to you, this mod is probably not for you.[/color][/b] There is no human-written edition.
[/color]


[size=4][b][color=#D6A24A]Compatibility, Stability & Support[/color][/b][/size]

[color=#D4D4D8]
CIGAR works at runtime through SKSE. No two heavily modded games are alike, so compatibility with every combination cannot be guaranteed; back up important saves before installing or updating SKSE plugins. Support covers the official, unmodified release.

When reporting an issue, please include the CIGAR, Skyrim and SKSE versions, [b]Documents/My Games/Skyrim Special Edition/SKSE/CIGAR.log[/b], and how to reproduce the problem.
[/color]


[center]
